      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Detectors the generator cannot reach",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Descriptor-free detectors that live behind cv2 CLASSES: SimpleBlobDetector, FastFeatureDetector, GFTTDetector and MSER. Each comes as a curated node - the raw cv2.* function wrappers cannot reach them (cv2_goodFeaturesToTrack returns bare points with no keypoint size or angle, and FAST has no function form at all).\n\nRow 1 - 'CV Detect Blobs' finds compact spots by sweeping EVERY threshold and keeping what stays stable, then filters by SHAPE (area / circularity / convexity / inertia). Each filter is driven by its own value: 0 means 'do not filter'.\nRow 2 (1st part) - FAST (unbounded, thousands per millisecond) \nRow 2 (2nd part) - 'CV Compute Descriptors' is the missing half of the Feature2D API: it describes keypoints that came from a detector with no descriptors of its own, so FAST corners can be matched with SIFT descriptors. Use the node's OWN keypoints output downstream - the descriptor drops border keypoints.\nRow 3 - GFTT Shi-Tomasi (bounded and evenly spread, the classic KLT seed) on the same image.\nRow 4 - MSER returns REGIONS, not points: the convex outlines go out as contours and the exact pixels as a mask."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
